{"id":"h1n1_09","name":"H1N1 新型流感爆發","date":"2009-04-24","cat":"pandemic","cat_name":"疫情","note":"墨西哥與美國通報疫情（週五），6 月 WHO 宣布大流行","approx":false,"background":{"note":"墨西哥與美國通報疫情（週五），6 月 WHO 宣布大流行","external":{"background":"新型 H1N1 流感自墨西哥擴散，WHO 6 月宣布大流行，墨西哥觀光受重創","notes":"查無全球層級的 H1N1 實測經濟損失總額（找過 World Bank、CDC/WHO、學術摘要）；World Bank 的 GDP 0.7–4.8% 是假設性大流行情境，不是 H1N1 實績，未採用。墨西哥兩個口徑（0.7% vs 1% GDP）並存，因未取得 CEPAL 專題報告原文，無法調和；0.7% 口徑的美元值未換算（沒有可引用的匯率來源）。","headline":{"usd_bn":9.111,"kind":"realized_loss","what":"墨西哥 2009 年疫情經濟損失 1,273.594 億披索，約 GDP 的 1%，為墨西哥史上損失最高的單一災害（CEPAL《流感 A H1N1 對墨西哥衝擊初步評估》；報導自帶美元值 $91.11 億；觀光佔 37%）","source":"Agencia Reforma（經 El Siglo de Torreón）2010-04-28《Es influenza el desastre más costoso en México》，轉述 CEPAL《Evaluación Preliminar del Impacto de la Influenza A H1N1 en México》","url":"https://www.elsiglodetorreon.com.mx/noticia/2010/es-influenza-el-desastre-mas-costoso-en-mexico.html"},"impacts":[{"what":"墨西哥 2009 年疫情經濟損失 1,273.594 億披索，約 GDP 的 1%，為墨西哥史上損失最高的單一災害（CEPAL《流感 A H1N1 對墨西哥衝擊初步評估》；報導自帶美元值 $91.11 億；觀光佔 37%）","usd_bn":9.111,"range_bn":null,"as_of":"2010","source":"Agencia Reforma（經 El Siglo de Torreón）2010-04-28《Es influenza el desastre más costoso en México》，轉述 CEPAL《Evaluación Preliminar del Impacto de la Influenza A H1N1 en México》","url":"https://www.elsiglodetorreon.com.mx/noticia/2010/es-influenza-el-desastre-mas-costoso-en-mexico.html","source_quality":"secondary","kind":"realized_loss"},{"what":"CEPAL（ECLAC）對墨西哥 2009 年疫情衝擊的另一口徑：約 GDP 的 0.7%（原文只給百分比，未給美元；墨西哥衛生部長 2009-11 亦稱 570 億披索＝0.7% GDP，Expansión 報導）","usd_bn":null,"range_bn":null,"as_of":"2010","source":"ECLAC, Economic Survey of Latin America and the Caribbean 2009-2010, Mexico chapter（'ECLAC estimates that the impact was equivalent to a loss of about 0.7% of GDP'）","url":"https://repositorio.cepal.org/server/api/core/bitstreams/8ee62d3b-ea5b-491e-9153-eed3b838819f/content","source_quality":"primary","kind":"realized_loss"}]}},"pre":{"lag":null,"months":[{"m":"2008-04","n":10,"on":